{"status":"completed","summary":"Inventory application is serving successfully on node1 TCP port 8181. SELinux remains Enforcing, Apache runs under httpd_t, port 8181 is mapped to http_port_t, and firewalld permits the port. Configuration and application content survived the mandatory node restart.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Apache HTTP Server.","Configured Apache to listen on TCP 8181.","Created the inventory application landing page.","Persistently assigned TCP 8181 to the SELinux http_port_t type.","Added runtime and permanent firewalld rules for TCP 8181.","Restarted node1 safely and verified recovery and persistence."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Serve the inventory application over TCP port 8181 while mandatory access control remains enforcing","command_ids":["cmd-6a11971490cc40ad","cmd-907474dede124b45"],"summary":"Before and after restart, SELinux reported Enforcing; Apache ran in httpd_t, listened on 8181, and returned the Inventory Application page with HTTP 200 through node1's managed IP. The http_port_t mapping and firewall allowance were present."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart sequence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-0db37066f107468b","cmd-4505c970d8554651","cmd-072fef8181a54eba","cmd-d4e5362dc8174dab","cmd-907474dede124b45"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was a70d7f83-6867-4c91-851d-7a1228689bb3; reboot was acknowledged; post-restart boot ID changed to dc326313-c2b3-40f9-aa97-17c422b1c2e7. The system reached running state, httpd recovered as active/enabled, SELinux remained Enforcing, TCP 8181 was listening, firewall and SELinux policy persisted, and the application returned HTTP 200."}]}
